1
00:00:07,825 --> 00:00:09,955
(Spice Rice Cake)

2
00:00:10,425 --> 00:00:14,625
(Space Rice Cake is closed today.)

3
00:00:14,995 --> 00:00:17,995
(Well, because I don't have to cook today...)

4
00:00:17,995 --> 00:00:19,565
(I almost finished all the food.)

5
00:00:20,165 --> 00:00:24,335
(They enjoy a relaxing tea time.)

6
00:00:24,975 --> 00:00:29,475
(The rice cakes come out great today.)

7
00:00:29,945 --> 00:00:32,045
(But the joy of having a day off didn't last long.)

8
00:00:32,275 --> 00:00:34,315
(Where did all the cameras go?)

9
00:00:34,645 --> 00:00:35,645
(It makes me anxious.)

10
00:00:35,645 --> 00:00:37,455
(Why don't I see any cameras?)

11
00:00:38,285 --> 00:00:41,055
(Something feels off outside.)

12
00:00:41,685 --> 00:00:45,095
(For some reason, their affection for Goheung deepens today.)

13
00:00:45,895 --> 00:00:51,195
(Something feels wrong, but they choose to enjoy their day off.)

14
00:00:51,395 --> 00:00:53,135
Are we going to the photo studio first?

15
00:00:53,135 --> 00:00:54,905
What... Are we going to the photo studio first?

16
00:00:54,905 --> 00:00:56,535
Yes, we're stopping by the photo studio, but first...

17
00:00:56,535 --> 00:00:59,005
While you were making the rice cakes,

18
00:00:59,175 --> 00:01:01,475
we got a call from the HQ.

19
00:01:02,045 --> 00:01:03,075
What did they say?

20
00:01:03,815 --> 00:01:05,315
- What's with that serious face?
- What did they say?

21
00:01:05,645 --> 00:01:06,945
- We need to leave.
- The HQ...

22
00:01:06,945 --> 00:01:09,515
I mean, you've been telling us some of the work issues.

23
00:01:09,515 --> 00:01:10,815
The POS system.

24
00:01:10,985 --> 00:01:13,855
(I really want the POS system!)

25
00:01:14,255 --> 00:01:15,585
(Please.)

26
00:01:15,785 --> 00:01:17,095
- Really?
- You wanted the POS system.

27
00:01:17,255 --> 00:01:18,555
- What else?
- I want a part-timer.

28
00:01:18,555 --> 00:01:19,925
- You wanted a part-timer.
- I really want that.

29
00:01:20,295 --> 00:01:22,625
(Can you get a part-timer for us?)

30
00:01:22,995 --> 00:01:24,635
(Post an ad on a secondhand market or something.)

31
00:01:24,935 --> 00:01:26,935
(Hire a part-timer!)

32
00:01:26,935 --> 00:01:28,005
(Come on!)

33
00:01:28,005 --> 00:01:29,765
- The tables make it hard to serve.
- The tables.

34
00:01:29,765 --> 00:01:31,275
And you also asked...

35
00:01:31,275 --> 00:01:32,735
- for a waiting area.
- Yes.

36
00:01:32,735 --> 00:01:35,375
- We told them about your requests.
- I see.

37
00:01:35,405 --> 00:01:38,015
And the HQ says that, since you've been working so hard,

38
00:01:38,215 --> 00:01:39,715
they want to grant your requests.

39
00:01:39,945 --> 00:01:41,345
That's what they said.

40
00:01:41,745 --> 00:01:44,285
Where has Young Ji been wanting to go since day one?

41
00:01:44,415 --> 00:01:45,415
Seoul.

42
00:01:45,485 --> 00:01:47,285
- Oh, I see... What?
- Seoul.

43
00:01:47,285 --> 00:01:48,855
You said you wanted to go to Seoul.

44
00:01:49,055 --> 00:01:50,925
- Why do you keep doing this to me?
- No way.

45
00:01:51,695 --> 00:01:54,725
I mean, why... I just want to go up above the sky.

46
00:01:54,725 --> 00:01:56,365
Why are you doing this to our king?

47
00:01:56,365 --> 00:01:57,995
- Why do you keep doing this to me?
- But just earlier...

48
00:01:57,995 --> 00:01:59,835
Only yesterday, you said you could...

49
00:01:59,835 --> 00:02:01,105
- run a restaurant in Seoul.
- Are we going to Seoul?

50
00:02:01,105 --> 00:02:02,965
(Are we going to Seoul?)

51
00:02:02,965 --> 00:02:05,335
(Can we go to Seoul?)

52
00:02:05,335 --> 00:02:06,835
This is how I feel, Mimi.

53
00:02:06,835 --> 00:02:09,075
(We're now good enough to run a restaurant in Seoul.)

54
00:02:09,605 --> 00:02:10,615
(Do you want to go to Seoul?)

55
00:02:10,615 --> 00:02:11,615
(Yes.)

56
00:02:11,715 --> 00:02:13,585
(She did go on about how she wanted to go to Seoul every day.)

57
00:02:13,915 --> 00:02:17,155
So the HQ opened up the second branch in Seoul.

58
00:02:17,155 --> 00:02:19,555
- What are you talking about? Now?
- This is ridiculous.

59
00:02:19,555 --> 00:02:20,785
- Why would you do that?
- Are we going to Seoul?

60
00:02:20,785 --> 00:02:22,225
Don't lie to us. Are we really going to Seoul?

61
00:02:22,225 --> 00:02:23,385
It's true. The second branch is...

62
00:02:23,385 --> 00:02:25,055
- Are we really going to Seoul?
- Come on. Don't lie to us.

63
00:02:25,055 --> 00:02:26,095
- It's only been four days...
- No wonder.

64
00:02:26,095 --> 00:02:27,125
- since we came here.
- No wonder.

65
00:02:27,125 --> 00:02:28,365
It's only been four days, but it's true.

66
00:02:28,365 --> 00:02:31,635
Since you guys wanted to go to a busy neighborhood,

67
00:02:31,635 --> 00:02:33,635
we picked a popular neighborhood, Yeonhui-dong.

68
00:02:35,265 --> 00:02:36,505
It's located in the middle of Yeonhui-dong.

69
00:02:36,505 --> 00:02:38,105
- Really?
- That's so close to my house.

70
00:02:38,105 --> 00:02:39,175
The second branch...

71
00:02:39,275 --> 00:02:41,405
(The youngest member is simply happy about going to Seoul.)

72
00:02:41,805 --> 00:02:44,315
- That's so close to my house.
- She's thinking of going home.

73
00:02:44,315 --> 00:02:46,315
But we provide shared housing for all of you...

74
00:02:46,315 --> 00:02:48,685
- Oh, right. I know.
- as an employee benefit.

75
00:02:48,685 --> 00:02:49,815
I want to stay with them in the same place.

76
00:02:49,815 --> 00:02:51,915
- But that's not the problem.
- Right. Let's stay together.

77
00:02:51,915 --> 00:02:53,925
- Why must we leave here?
- Exactly. I...

78
00:02:53,925 --> 00:02:55,555
I just got used to this place.

79
00:02:55,555 --> 00:02:57,195
- We have everything in the kitchen.
- Exactly. We just got used to...

80
00:02:57,195 --> 00:02:58,625
- working in that kitchen.
- We got used to working there.

81
00:02:58,625 --> 00:03:01,095
- I'm not doing this!
- Hold on.

82
00:03:01,365 --> 00:03:04,635
- Let's go on strike.
- Hey.

83
00:03:04,835 --> 00:03:06,065
- Hey.
- Why?

84
00:03:06,065 --> 00:03:07,065
- We're going on strike!
- But why...

85
00:03:07,065 --> 00:03:08,805
- But Young Ji, you said...
- You asked us to send you there.

86
00:03:08,805 --> 00:03:10,235
That has nothing to do with this.

87
00:03:10,235 --> 00:03:11,575
You said you wanted to go to Seoul.

88
00:03:11,575 --> 00:03:12,805
- That's why they arranged this.
- I mean...

89
00:03:12,805 --> 00:03:15,275
- If I had suggested the US...
- We just got used to working here.

90
00:03:15,275 --> 00:03:17,115
Would we be going to the US if that was the case?

91
00:03:17,115 --> 00:03:18,575
- Yes, we were going to do that.
- You see...

92
00:03:18,575 --> 00:03:20,785
- We would've arranged that.
- Of course.

93
00:03:20,785 --> 00:03:22,215
- I mean...
- They might change the plan again.

94
00:03:22,215 --> 00:03:23,785
We might have to deal with another challenge.

95
00:03:23,785 --> 00:03:24,985
- Do you want to go to the US?
- That brat...

96
00:03:25,155 --> 00:03:26,515
Young Ji, do you want to go to the US?

97
00:03:26,685 --> 00:03:28,255
Didn't you just say you wanted to go to the US?

98
00:03:28,685 --> 00:03:30,725
- Your Highness, my dear princess...
- How about we...

99
00:03:30,725 --> 00:03:31,825
travel across the US?

100
00:03:31,825 --> 00:03:35,195
Please keep your mouth shut, Your Highness.

101
00:03:35,195 --> 00:03:36,425
I love the idea of going to Seoul.

102
00:03:37,435 --> 00:03:39,795
We should leave right now so we can start working there.

103
00:03:39,795 --> 00:03:41,005
- Right now?
- We're going to Seoul today?

104
00:03:41,005 --> 00:03:42,335
- My gosh. Hang on a second.
- We're going to Seoul now.

105
00:03:42,535 --> 00:03:44,405
(She grabs the back of her neck in disbelief.)

106
00:03:44,735 --> 00:03:46,775
(It's heartbreaking and funny at the same time.)

107
00:03:47,475 --> 00:03:48,645
- Hold on.
- Are you okay?

108
00:03:48,645 --> 00:03:51,815
I haven't even said goodbye to the stove yet.

109
00:03:51,815 --> 00:03:52,875
You can do that now.

110
00:03:52,875 --> 00:03:54,945
I have a question for you guys.

111
00:03:55,145 --> 00:03:57,485
Why is it a challenge for the kitchen team...

112
00:03:57,485 --> 00:03:58,785
to work in Seoul, not Goheung?

113
00:03:58,785 --> 00:03:59,785
Listen to me.

114
00:03:59,785 --> 00:04:01,655
We just got used to...

115
00:04:01,655 --> 00:04:02,985
- how things work here.
- Okay.

116
00:04:02,985 --> 00:04:04,825
- And I got attached to this place.
- Okay.

117
00:04:04,825 --> 00:04:06,495
- I can't leave here.
- My point exactly.

118
00:04:06,625 --> 00:04:09,365
I've only just settled into my work here.

119
00:04:09,365 --> 00:04:12,265
Since you stabilized the business in such a short time,

120
00:04:12,795 --> 00:04:14,735
the HQ wants you to do the same for the second branch.

121
00:04:15,235 --> 00:04:16,735
They want you to work your magic there too.

122
00:04:17,375 --> 00:04:19,805
You need to expand your business if you want to succeed, you know.

123
00:04:20,675 --> 00:04:23,375
How the service team is okay with this makes me even more upset.

124
00:04:24,975 --> 00:04:26,275
They're fine with this decision.

125
00:04:26,375 --> 00:04:27,985
You can even use the POS system there.

126
00:04:27,985 --> 00:04:29,445
That's really great. We're just so happy.

127
00:04:29,445 --> 00:04:31,615
And we'll probably have standing tables there.

128
00:04:31,855 --> 00:04:34,025
- Then give us just one minute.
- Go and say goodbye.

129
00:04:34,025 --> 00:04:35,225
Say goodbye to the stove.

130
00:04:35,655 --> 00:04:39,355
(Rushing)

131
00:04:40,425 --> 00:04:41,495
Mimi.

132
00:04:41,495 --> 00:04:42,495
(It feels empty in the kitchen.)

133
00:04:42,495 --> 00:04:43,525
Guys.

134
00:04:44,095 --> 00:04:46,495
- Take care.
- Guys.

135
00:04:46,495 --> 00:04:48,705
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye, guys.

136
00:04:48,705 --> 00:04:49,735
One last time...

137
00:04:50,805 --> 00:04:51,875
Let's have a look at them for the last time.

138
00:04:51,875 --> 00:04:53,205
(They're saying goodbye to each and every ingredient.)

139
00:04:53,335 --> 00:04:54,645
Guys.

140
00:04:55,105 --> 00:04:56,975
Goodbye, deep-fryer.

141
00:04:57,075 --> 00:04:58,515
I can't believe this.

142
00:05:00,175 --> 00:05:02,445
I can't leave.

143
00:05:02,515 --> 00:05:05,155
I've grown so attached to this place.

144
00:05:06,015 --> 00:05:09,125
Why would everything I say come true?

145
00:05:09,755 --> 00:05:12,425
What did I do so wrong?

146
00:05:12,825 --> 00:05:15,295
You know that's not what I meant by "going to Seoul."

147
00:05:15,925 --> 00:05:18,535
Why would they lie on the ground?

148
00:05:19,535 --> 00:05:20,705
(Meanwhile, Yu Jin brings something with her.)

149
00:05:20,705 --> 00:05:21,865
I really like the idea.

150
00:05:22,435 --> 00:05:23,665
I'm going to take some photos.

151
00:05:23,665 --> 00:05:25,535
(The service team takes photos to capture the memories.)

152
00:05:25,735 --> 00:05:26,905
Let's go to the beach.

153
00:05:27,275 --> 00:05:28,505
- To the beach?
- Yes.

154
00:05:30,105 --> 00:05:31,375
This is legendary.

155
00:05:31,375 --> 00:05:32,815
- Was it in the frame? Okay.
- Step back further.

156
00:05:33,315 --> 00:05:36,415
(This part-timer is used to posing for photos.)

157
00:05:36,485 --> 00:05:37,955
- Was it okay?
- Look at the photo I just took.

158
00:05:45,955 --> 00:05:48,625
(She's so good at taking photos.)

159
00:05:48,795 --> 00:05:51,095
This vibe... This is what I'm talking about.

160
00:05:51,535 --> 00:05:53,595
(This time, Yu Jin takes photos of Eun Ji.)

161
00:05:53,595 --> 00:05:54,765
(Chuckling)

162
00:05:54,765 --> 00:05:56,005
You look stylish, Eun Ji.

163
00:05:58,605 --> 00:06:01,175
(While the service team is busy posing and taking photos...)

164
00:06:01,745 --> 00:06:04,545
How can I leave all these behind and go to Seoul?

165
00:06:04,545 --> 00:06:06,715
There's good equipment in Seoul too.

166
00:06:06,715 --> 00:06:09,145
So I should just abandon my beloved equipment here?

167
00:06:09,815 --> 00:06:11,655
How am I supposed to abandon my precious equipment...

168
00:06:11,655 --> 00:06:12,655
(Groaning)

169
00:06:12,785 --> 00:06:15,055
(Clutching the back of her neck to control her rising blood pressure)

170
00:06:15,185 --> 00:06:16,955
Hold that pose and look down.

171
00:06:17,155 --> 00:06:18,595
Make it look like you're tucking your hair behind your ear.

172
00:06:18,695 --> 00:06:19,825
Your Majesty,

173
00:06:19,825 --> 00:06:21,565
- I beg you to understand them.
- How dare you...

174
00:06:21,565 --> 00:06:23,195
treat your king this way?

175
00:06:23,525 --> 00:06:25,135
Do we have more tables there?

176
00:06:25,335 --> 00:06:26,935
- Probably.
- You'll see when you get there.

177
00:06:27,665 --> 00:06:28,905
Find out when you get there.

178
00:06:28,905 --> 00:06:30,535
Let's rip this off and pack it with us.

179
00:06:30,535 --> 00:06:31,635
- Like this.
- Yes.

180
00:06:31,635 --> 00:06:33,235
- Just lift it up.
- Like this.

181
00:06:33,235 --> 00:06:35,075
We have even better ones there.

182
00:06:35,445 --> 00:06:36,675
It has to be this one.

183
00:06:36,675 --> 00:06:38,215
Exactly. I can't use any other stove.

184
00:06:38,575 --> 00:06:40,715
Wait. They're taking photos.

185
00:06:40,715 --> 00:06:42,815
They'll take some photos for about ten minutes...

186
00:06:42,815 --> 00:06:44,015
and go to pack their stuff.

187
00:06:44,015 --> 00:06:46,785
(Closing her eyes for photos)

188
00:06:46,785 --> 00:06:49,185
Let's hurry up and have some photos taken.

189
00:06:49,725 --> 00:06:51,895
Goodbye, my friend.

190
00:06:51,895 --> 00:06:53,095
(To the kitchen equipment)

191
00:06:53,455 --> 00:06:55,865
My beloved friend.

192
00:06:56,295 --> 00:06:57,435
For some reason, the rice cake...

193
00:06:58,035 --> 00:06:59,635
It's still warm.

194
00:06:59,635 --> 00:07:00,905
What do we do?

195
00:07:00,905 --> 00:07:02,335
(And then she cries her heart out again.)

196
00:07:02,505 --> 00:07:04,505
What's wrong with the kitchen team?

197
00:07:05,135 --> 00:07:06,605
(She feels ticked off by them for no reason.)

198
00:07:06,605 --> 00:07:07,805
What are you doing right now?

199
00:07:07,805 --> 00:07:10,205
(What are you doing right now?)

200
00:07:10,275 --> 00:07:11,515
Say goodbye and come on out.

201
00:07:11,515 --> 00:07:13,345
We have to run the second branch...

202
00:07:13,345 --> 00:07:15,385
(Screaming)

203
00:07:15,585 --> 00:07:17,455
Hurry up and pack your... Hurry up and come out already.

204
00:07:17,685 --> 00:07:18,885
Come on out.

205
00:07:18,885 --> 00:07:20,285
(She walks toward her beloved kitchen tools again.)

206
00:07:21,085 --> 00:07:24,095
You worked here only for four days. Why are you...

207
00:07:24,325 --> 00:07:25,995
We have those in Seoul too.

208
00:07:25,995 --> 00:07:27,695
Young Ji and Mimi!

209
00:07:28,395 --> 00:07:29,495
- The cleaver?
- Yes.

210
00:07:29,495 --> 00:07:30,495
Why would you pack the cleaver?

211
00:07:30,495 --> 00:07:31,735
We have a cleaver in Seoul too.

212
00:07:31,735 --> 00:07:33,695
All right. Let's get going.

213
00:07:34,035 --> 00:07:35,365
Let's go home now.

214
00:07:35,705 --> 00:07:37,975
- Are we really leaving like this?
- Yes.

215
00:07:38,205 --> 00:07:40,305
We can have the photoshoot in Seoul if you want.

216
00:07:40,305 --> 00:07:41,975
- We can hang out here a little...
- Okay.

217
00:07:41,975 --> 00:07:43,375
and just stop by the general store. What do you want to do?

218
00:07:43,705 --> 00:07:45,445
- Won't you do the photoshoot?
- I'll do that.

219
00:07:46,375 --> 00:07:47,445
Mother.

220
00:07:48,315 --> 00:07:49,345
- Let's get going.
- Let's go.

221
00:07:49,885 --> 00:07:52,255
(She reluctantly steps out through the gate.)

222
00:07:52,455 --> 00:07:54,225
(She grabs the open sign on her way out.)

223
00:07:54,585 --> 00:07:55,585
One, two, three.

224
00:07:56,255 --> 00:08:00,025
(They bring the sidewalk sign inside.)

225
00:08:00,025 --> 00:08:02,065
We're heading to the second branch.

226
00:08:02,365 --> 00:08:04,365
- Goodbye.
- We're going to the second branch.

227
00:08:04,535 --> 00:08:06,235
Goodbye, Goheung.

228
00:08:06,695 --> 00:08:08,805
- Let's go to the second branch.
- Okay.

229
00:08:09,305 --> 00:08:11,675
You need to pack your bag quickly so you can enjoy shopping...

230
00:08:11,675 --> 00:08:13,405
and do the photoshoot. Let's go.

231
00:08:13,975 --> 00:08:15,075
We can "enjoy shopping."

232
00:08:15,075 --> 00:08:16,375
What's the point of shopping at the general store?

233
00:08:16,375 --> 00:08:18,515
All their stuff has the Goheung vibe.

234
00:08:18,515 --> 00:08:20,915
Guys, let's just stop by the photo studio.

235
00:08:20,915 --> 00:08:22,645
We won't even get to visit the general store.

236
00:08:23,345 --> 00:08:24,415
Are we just leaving like this?

237
00:08:24,715 --> 00:08:28,155
The stuff at the general store has the Goheung vibe. Right, Yu Jin?

238
00:08:28,155 --> 00:08:29,455
- Absolutely.
- They have the Goheung vibe.

239
00:08:29,455 --> 00:08:30,995
Are you going to buy some chairs and take them to Seoul?

240
00:08:30,995 --> 00:08:32,025
We don't need to stop by there.

241
00:08:32,025 --> 00:08:34,425
How do we carry all those to the airport?

242
00:08:34,895 --> 00:08:37,125
- All right.
- Good. Let's not visit the store.

243
00:08:37,125 --> 00:08:39,735
- Then we...
- We'll only visit the photo studio.

244
00:08:39,735 --> 00:08:43,265
Father, why are you so powerless over them?

245
00:08:43,265 --> 00:08:45,335
I wanted to have a look around the store.

246
00:08:45,335 --> 00:08:47,705
Since we're going to sleep together,

247
00:08:47,975 --> 00:08:50,175
I'll tell you about the store at night.

248
00:08:51,145 --> 00:08:52,475
- We're going to sleep together.
- Will you describe it vividly?

249
00:08:52,475 --> 00:08:54,815
- So I can picture it in my mind?
- I'll make sure of it.

250
00:08:54,915 --> 00:08:58,415
I'll be by your side one night, and by Mimi's side the next.

251
00:08:58,855 --> 00:08:59,885
And the next day...

252
00:09:00,485 --> 00:09:02,725
- We'll leave at 3pm, guys.
- Got it.

253
00:09:03,085 --> 00:09:04,095
Hurry up and come in.

254
00:09:04,455 --> 00:09:06,125
(Everyone is rushing inside to pack their bags.)

255
00:09:06,125 --> 00:09:08,025
Come on in already. We don't have time for that.

256
00:09:09,065 --> 00:09:12,095
(She sighs deeply and plops down on the floor.)

257
00:09:12,395 --> 00:09:13,465
I feel so hollow.

258
00:09:14,235 --> 00:09:17,205
Mimi, take off your gloves and mask.

259
00:09:17,575 --> 00:09:19,375
- Eun Ji.
- You feel so hollow?

260
00:09:19,375 --> 00:09:20,405
(She feels bad for Mimi.)

261
00:09:20,405 --> 00:09:21,475
Are you tearing up?

262
00:09:21,745 --> 00:09:23,775
(She's practically wailing.)

263
00:09:23,775 --> 00:09:24,815
What's the matter?

264
00:09:24,815 --> 00:09:27,175
It's good that we get to introduce our food to people in Seoul, right?

265
00:09:27,175 --> 00:09:28,785
- That's true.
- Right.

266
00:09:29,315 --> 00:09:31,385
I know you're right. You're absolutely right.

267
00:09:31,755 --> 00:09:34,785
- You know that, but still feel sad.
- That's right.

268
00:09:35,485 --> 00:09:38,125
Gosh. I don't want to leave.

269
00:09:38,825 --> 00:09:40,055
Why are you so sad, Young Ji?

270
00:09:41,225 --> 00:09:42,265
Are you that upset?

271
00:09:43,195 --> 00:09:45,865
Seriously, why am I so upset? I really don't want to leave.

272
00:09:45,865 --> 00:09:46,935
(She's sad to go, right when she settled into the work here.)

273
00:09:46,935 --> 00:09:48,735
I'm so used to working in that kitchen.

274
00:09:48,735 --> 00:09:50,605
- You have a lot of love in you.
- Right.

275
00:09:51,075 --> 00:09:53,035
I just got used to working here.

276
00:09:53,575 --> 00:09:55,375
I'm sure they'll set up the new kitchen...

277
00:09:55,375 --> 00:09:58,015
the exact same way as the one here.

278
00:09:58,375 --> 00:10:02,945
(The 2 kitchen team members managed to pack up and step outside.)

279
00:10:03,685 --> 00:10:06,385
At least we're not going overseas. That's a relief, right?

280
00:10:06,785 --> 00:10:08,055
Maybe that would be better.

281
00:10:08,985 --> 00:10:10,995
- Don't say such a thing.
- Got it.

282
00:10:10,995 --> 00:10:12,795
- Maybe that would be better?
- All right.

283
00:10:13,325 --> 00:10:14,395
Why only my words...

284
00:10:15,965 --> 00:10:17,735
Why do only my words turn into reality?

285
00:10:17,735 --> 00:10:19,735
(Why do only my words turn into reality?)

286
00:10:20,135 --> 00:10:22,805
- Hello.
- Hello.

287
00:10:22,805 --> 00:10:23,805
(Getting on the bus)

288
00:10:24,335 --> 00:10:25,605
(The 2 kitchen team members drag their heavy feet.)

289
00:10:26,075 --> 00:10:27,175
- Hello.
- Get on the bus.

290
00:10:28,005 --> 00:10:29,005
She's one cold-hearted woman.

291
00:10:30,305 --> 00:10:31,415
Hello.

292
00:10:31,515 --> 00:10:33,615
Why are you looking so sad?

293
00:10:33,775 --> 00:10:36,585
Good job, you guys. It's always hard to say goodbye to what you love.

294
00:10:37,115 --> 00:10:40,155
Saying goodbye is never easy, but let's try to do it with a smile.

295
00:10:40,155 --> 00:10:41,185
I'm okay.

296
00:10:41,185 --> 00:10:45,595
- This parting will break our hearts - Break our hearts

297
00:10:45,795 --> 00:10:49,365
(But it will be graceful)

298
00:10:50,965 --> 00:10:55,065
(Saying goodbye to Goheung breaks our hearts.)

299
00:10:55,965 --> 00:11:00,105
(But we say goodbye to welcome another challenge!)

300
00:11:00,805 --> 00:11:04,775
(I wouldn't mind regretting making rice cakes.)

301
00:11:05,175 --> 00:11:09,615
(So we're saying goodbye to Goheung.)

302
00:11:10,085 --> 00:11:15,955
(Goodbye to the rainy day when it poured)

303
00:11:16,485 --> 00:11:19,925
(Goodbye to the customers who came all the way here)

304
00:11:19,925 --> 00:11:24,135
(Goodbye to the customers who came all the way here)

305
00:11:24,395 --> 00:11:29,135
(Goodbye to those little moments we shared)

306
00:11:29,465 --> 00:11:31,905
(The Goheung branch was meaningful as it was our first restaurant.)

307
00:11:32,335 --> 00:11:34,405
(Goodbye)

308
00:11:36,905 --> 00:11:39,315
(Closed for business)

309
00:11:39,975 --> 00:11:41,615
Are we going to stop by the photo studio?

310
00:11:41,615 --> 00:11:44,515
Yes, we'll stop by the photo studio and then head to the airport.

311
00:11:45,315 --> 00:11:47,415
I want to go straight to the airport.

312
00:11:48,155 --> 00:11:50,125
- Won't you do the photoshoot?
- I will.

313
00:11:51,355 --> 00:11:52,425
(I should do what I have to do.)

314
00:11:52,425 --> 00:11:53,455
You will, right?

315
00:11:55,295 --> 00:11:57,565
This is how little kids behave when they're sulky.

316
00:11:57,935 --> 00:12:00,065
- "So you really won't do it?"
- "I will."

317
00:12:00,065 --> 00:12:01,465
(Mimi, the kid, is sulky after losing her restaurant.)

318
00:12:02,305 --> 00:12:03,405
We're leaving.

319
00:12:04,705 --> 00:12:06,175
What's the final tally for our sales?

320
00:12:07,135 --> 00:12:08,805
- Is it 1,200 dollars?
- It's over 1,000 dollars.

321
00:12:08,805 --> 00:12:09,805
Is it about 1,300 dollars?

322
00:12:09,905 --> 00:12:11,545
What are we going to do with that money?

323
00:12:11,545 --> 00:12:14,385
- Let's put it into SK Hynix.
- Let's do that.

324
00:12:14,385 --> 00:12:15,415
Let's invest the money in stocks.

325
00:12:16,415 --> 00:12:17,915
They say ETFs are better.

326
00:12:17,985 --> 00:12:21,325
- Right.
- Let's say we have 1,300 dollars.

327
00:12:21,325 --> 00:12:22,485
How much is that if we split it four ways?

328
00:12:23,155 --> 00:12:24,225
It's...

329
00:12:24,225 --> 00:12:27,295
But SK Hynix might reach 160,000 dollars a share in a year.

330
00:12:27,625 --> 00:12:29,825
I mean, we don't have much of seed money.

331
00:12:29,825 --> 00:12:31,195
We're going to make more money this week...

332
00:12:31,195 --> 00:12:32,465
- We'll put it all into SK Hynix?
- Yes.

333
00:12:32,865 --> 00:12:34,135
Let's buy the stocks when we make 3,000 or 4,000 dollars.

334
00:12:34,465 --> 00:12:37,005
- Will you execute the trades?
- Yes.

335
00:12:37,875 --> 00:12:39,275
I do want to get a new phone.

336
00:12:39,275 --> 00:12:40,505
(Chuckling)

337
00:12:40,835 --> 00:12:42,605
- You bought that one recently.
- It's all cracked.

338
00:12:42,605 --> 00:12:44,075
(Use of Funds 2: Buying a new phone for Yu Jin)

339
00:12:44,075 --> 00:12:45,845
- It's too heavy.
- You can put a phone case on it.

340
00:12:46,315 --> 00:12:47,345
It'll be too heavy.

341
00:12:48,615 --> 00:12:49,845
Is going caseless a trend...

342
00:12:49,845 --> 00:12:52,515
among young people these days?

343
00:12:52,515 --> 00:12:53,555
You're not on the younger side.

344
00:12:53,555 --> 00:12:56,625
- I'm old-fashioned.
- You're on the older side.

345
00:12:57,225 --> 00:12:58,925
- I'm on the older side.
- I'm young and trendy.

346
00:12:59,395 --> 00:13:01,625
- Is this considered trendy?
- I'm old-fashioned...

347
00:13:01,625 --> 00:13:03,525
- This is old-fashioned too.
- No, that's...

348
00:13:04,065 --> 00:13:06,095
Mimi got her feelings hurt so many times today.

349
00:13:06,395 --> 00:13:08,405
(The backstabbing staff and ruthlessly blunt younger members)

350
00:13:08,405 --> 00:13:09,565
You don't have to say she's old-fashioned.

351
00:13:10,935 --> 00:13:12,005
Mimi...

352
00:13:12,005 --> 00:13:13,075
(Punishing)

353
00:13:13,235 --> 00:13:15,105
- It's so funny that Mimi said...
- The temperature is...

354
00:13:15,105 --> 00:13:17,405
she wanted to open the restaurant today.

355
00:13:17,745 --> 00:13:19,515
When will you take your mask off, Young Ji?

356
00:13:20,575 --> 00:13:22,115
I'm going to keep it on a bit longer.

357
00:13:22,115 --> 00:13:24,045
She needs someone else to do it for her. Eun Ji can do it.

358
00:13:24,045 --> 00:13:25,915
I thought you would keep it on too.

359
00:13:25,915 --> 00:13:28,425
- Eun Ji helped me take it off.
- Yes, I did.

360
00:13:29,325 --> 00:13:31,525
- Give me some belly rubs.
- Why?

361
00:13:31,995 --> 00:13:33,025
So I can feel at ease.

362
00:13:33,125 --> 00:13:34,825
(She's so worried about working in Seoul that she might develop IBS.)

363
00:13:34,825 --> 00:13:35,865
Mimi...

364
00:13:35,865 --> 00:13:38,735
Mimi just asked for belly rubs so she could feel at ease.

365
00:13:39,995 --> 00:13:41,465
(Rubbing her belly)

366
00:13:41,835 --> 00:13:43,065
(Falling)

367
00:13:43,335 --> 00:13:45,575
Gosh, you shouldn't have brought those utensils.

368
00:13:46,605 --> 00:13:49,205
- Did it fall down?
- It fell down, Young Ji.

369
00:13:49,205 --> 00:13:50,575
- Why would you...
- You weren't even holding it.

370
00:13:50,575 --> 00:13:52,415
How are you going to board the plane with all that stuff?

371
00:13:52,675 --> 00:13:55,215
They're going to set off the metal detector repeatedly.

372
00:13:55,215 --> 00:13:57,415
(How could you say that right in front of my utensils?)

373
00:13:57,415 --> 00:13:58,915
- Seriously.
- What's wrong with you?

374
00:13:58,915 --> 00:14:01,855
You can easily find those at any dollar store.

375
00:14:02,355 --> 00:14:04,225
Why did you bring them with you?

376
00:14:05,125 --> 00:14:06,625
I couldn't just abandon my hometown friends.

377
00:14:07,155 --> 00:14:10,025
Should I abandon them because there are smarter ones in Seoul?

378
00:14:10,025 --> 00:14:11,135
Just take them with you.

379
00:14:11,935 --> 00:14:13,965
We were going to buy a hose at that store.

380
00:14:13,965 --> 00:14:15,865
- And a large basin.
- Exactly.

381
00:14:15,865 --> 00:14:17,305
Is that the general store?

382
00:14:17,305 --> 00:14:19,135
- No, it's a hardware store.
- No, it's...

383
00:14:19,575 --> 00:14:21,605
- It's a hardware store.
- They sell toilets?

384
00:14:22,375 --> 00:14:24,245
- There's a sauna over there.
- It's on your right side.

385
00:14:24,245 --> 00:14:27,315
- Y Sauna.
- Right, there's Y Sauna too.

386
00:14:27,785 --> 00:14:30,585
There are so many stores here. Isn't it like a whole new world?

387
00:14:30,815 --> 00:14:32,585
- Yes, it is.
- It's amazing.

388
00:14:32,815 --> 00:14:35,485
- We're here.
- Let's get off the bus now.

389
00:14:35,925 --> 00:14:38,125
Grab what you need for the photos when you get off the bus, okay?

390
00:14:38,125 --> 00:14:39,195
- Okay.
- Got it.

391
00:14:39,655 --> 00:14:41,065
- Hello.
- Hello.

392
00:14:41,065 --> 00:14:43,695
- Hello.
- Hello. It's nice to meet you all.

393
00:14:43,695 --> 00:14:45,935
We're here to take a family photo, just like this one.

394
00:14:45,935 --> 00:14:47,935
- Which one?
- This one right here.

395
00:14:48,265 --> 00:14:49,705
Oh, would you like the family photo theme?

396
00:14:49,705 --> 00:14:51,705
- Like this. With this background.
- Yes. I like this background.

397
00:14:51,705 --> 00:14:53,105
Young Ji, how about you wear this?

398
00:14:53,735 --> 00:14:54,805
I want to wear it.

399
00:14:55,145 --> 00:14:56,405
How about Young Ji wears this?

400
00:14:57,145 --> 00:15:00,015
(Young Ji immediately puts it on, giving off middle-aged man vibes.)

401
00:15:00,445 --> 00:15:03,545
(Yu Jin is glamming up too.)

402
00:15:04,045 --> 00:15:05,055
(Mimi brought her own prop.)

403
00:15:05,055 --> 00:15:06,085
It's good, right?

404
00:15:06,685 --> 00:15:08,425
(The photoshoot begins.)

405
00:15:09,185 --> 00:15:11,395
Don't try to look pretty. Try to look sentimental.

406
00:15:12,155 --> 00:15:14,565
(A sentimental smile?)

407
00:15:15,625 --> 00:15:18,135
Can you move the ladle a bit to the side?

408
00:15:18,735 --> 00:15:19,835
Move the ladle...

409
00:15:20,595 --> 00:15:21,665
One, two.

410
00:15:22,005 --> 00:15:23,635
One more time. One, two.

411
00:15:24,335 --> 00:15:25,805
(Closed for business)

412
00:15:25,805 --> 00:15:26,835
I'll take it.

413
00:15:26,835 --> 00:15:30,245
(Only the Goheung branch is closed.)

414
00:15:30,245 --> 00:15:31,945
- Your expression looks better now.
- One, two.

415
00:15:31,945 --> 00:15:34,685
(We still have the Seoul branch to run.)

416
00:15:34,945 --> 00:15:37,145
(Checking the photos)

417
00:15:37,345 --> 00:15:38,415
What's with that face?

418
00:15:40,215 --> 00:15:41,585
Why did you show your teeth like that?

419
00:15:41,725 --> 00:15:43,085
(She expressed her sadness by showing her teeth.)

420
00:15:43,085 --> 00:15:44,085
We're holding hands.

421
00:15:45,125 --> 00:15:46,355
I like this photo.

422
00:15:46,695 --> 00:15:48,895
I like... It's a great photo.

423
00:15:48,895 --> 00:15:49,965
I really like this one.

424
00:15:50,595 --> 00:15:52,895
The three of you have such glowing skin.

425
00:15:56,335 --> 00:15:58,005
Did you not apply lotion this morning?

426
00:15:58,405 --> 00:15:59,605
- Who?
- You, Young Ji.

427
00:15:59,605 --> 00:16:01,205
- I'm wearing makeup too.
- It's just...

428
00:16:01,505 --> 00:16:03,975
Your skin looks natural and smooth.

429
00:16:05,045 --> 00:16:07,315
- It's cute. The size is different.
- One of each.

430
00:16:08,215 --> 00:16:10,285
Let's make sure we never lose this photo.

431
00:16:10,285 --> 00:16:11,655
- Let's keep it safe.
- Okay.

432
00:16:11,655 --> 00:16:13,055
(What kind of memories will they make in Seoul?)

433
00:16:13,415 --> 00:16:16,855
(Yeosu Airport)

434
00:16:17,285 --> 00:16:19,855
(The Earth Arcaders arrived at Yeosu Airport.)

435
00:16:19,995 --> 00:16:25,065
(They boarded the flight carrying the utensils and the open sign.)

436
00:16:25,335 --> 00:16:27,195
(Departure: Yeosu Airport)

437
00:16:27,465 --> 00:16:29,135
(Arrival: Gimpo International Airport)

438
00:16:30,005 --> 00:16:31,035
(They set off for the Seoul branch!)

439
00:16:31,035 --> 00:16:32,435
Gosh, this is insane.

440
00:16:32,535 --> 00:16:35,345
I was just selling tteokbokki in Goheung, but now I'm here...

441
00:16:35,345 --> 00:16:37,005
This must be a dream. Isn't it?

442
00:16:37,005 --> 00:16:38,245
- It's a dream, right?
- It's a dream.

443
00:16:38,245 --> 00:16:40,715
- This is ridiculous, seriously.
- I just took a nap, right?

444
00:16:40,715 --> 00:16:43,215
But what am I wearing? What are these?

445
00:16:43,285 --> 00:16:44,345
(They were in Goheung just 2 hours ago.)

446
00:16:44,345 --> 00:16:47,255
- This is...
- We're closed for business.

447
00:16:47,315 --> 00:16:50,525
A lot of new things have been set up at the second branch.

448
00:16:50,525 --> 00:16:52,225
- I'm so excited.
- We'll give you a little tour...

449
00:16:52,225 --> 00:16:53,995
- and explain everything to you.
- Okay.

450
00:16:54,395 --> 00:16:56,265
Is there anything you're expecting to see there?

451
00:16:56,965 --> 00:16:58,065
- What we're expecting to see there?
- Yes.

452
00:16:58,435 --> 00:17:00,095
- A robot that can do a flip.
- Sorry?

453
00:17:00,765 --> 00:17:02,965
(Young Ji is dreaming of a state-of-the-art restaurant.)

454
00:17:02,965 --> 00:17:05,175
I wanted a robot...

455
00:17:05,875 --> 00:17:08,575
Is there anything else you want to see there?

456
00:17:08,575 --> 00:17:10,105
- No.
- Nothing else?

457
00:17:10,105 --> 00:17:12,845
I'll be happy if we just have the POS system.

458
00:17:12,845 --> 00:17:15,315
- Just the POS system?
- It'll solve all the problems.

459
00:17:16,215 --> 00:17:17,615
We won't be embarrassed...

460
00:17:17,615 --> 00:17:19,785
in front of the customers anymore.

461
00:17:19,785 --> 00:17:21,185
The POS system sounds great.

462
00:17:21,185 --> 00:17:23,225
Do we have a couple more serving carts?

463
00:17:23,225 --> 00:17:24,285
- Serving carts?
- Yes.

464
00:17:24,285 --> 00:17:25,825
The one you used in Goheung was too loud.

465
00:17:25,925 --> 00:17:29,125
(The street lit up brightly while they were sharing their wishes.)

466
00:17:29,865 --> 00:17:32,465
- Guys, this neighborhood is...
- We're actually in Seoul.

467
00:17:32,465 --> 00:17:33,835
- There's O Store.
- This is a totally different world.

468
00:17:34,035 --> 00:17:36,135
You're right. Look at that, guys.

469
00:17:36,135 --> 00:17:37,805
We were in the countryside.

470
00:17:38,205 --> 00:17:40,675
Hey, we're in the city now. What should we do?

471
00:17:40,675 --> 00:17:43,105
- It sure is so bright.
- It's bright, indeed.

472
00:17:43,105 --> 00:17:45,345
Night has already fallen, but it's still so bright.

473
00:17:45,345 --> 00:17:47,115
You're right. Girls, what do we do about this?

474
00:17:47,115 --> 00:17:50,015
(Seoul)

475
00:17:50,185 --> 00:17:53,955
(With a population of over 9 million)

476
00:17:53,955 --> 00:17:57,725
(A place packed with countless people)

477
00:17:57,925 --> 00:18:01,695
(Just as bustling as it is crowded)

478
00:18:01,825 --> 00:18:09,135
(Filled with different vibrant landmarks...)

479
00:18:09,205 --> 00:18:13,005
(and dazzling culture)

480
00:18:13,175 --> 00:18:16,075
(In this complex city of Seoul)

481
00:18:16,075 --> 00:18:19,445
(The neighborhood where Earth Arcaders run their business)

482
00:18:20,815 --> 00:18:22,185
(Yeonhui-dong)

483
00:18:24,915 --> 00:18:27,485
(Between low-rise buildings and old alleyways)

484
00:18:27,485 --> 00:18:32,895
(You'll find trendy restaurants everywhere.)

485
00:18:33,025 --> 00:18:35,225
(The neighborhood is constantly bustling...)

486
00:18:35,225 --> 00:18:37,865
(with food lovers.)

487
00:18:38,065 --> 00:18:40,765
(What kind of food experience will Space Rice Cake introduce?)

488
00:18:41,095 --> 00:18:43,365
There's Shinchon Central Baptist Church.

489
00:18:43,365 --> 00:18:44,905
(The Mapo-gu resident is starting to get excited.)

490
00:18:45,105 --> 00:18:46,575
If you go up this way,

491
00:18:46,575 --> 00:18:48,175
there's a nice charcoal dry sauna in Sinchon.

492
00:18:48,175 --> 00:18:50,175
- There's a charcoal sauna?
- Yes.

493
00:18:50,175 --> 00:18:52,445
This place looks familiar. Wait a minute.

494
00:18:54,115 --> 00:18:55,115
It's that gimbap restaurant.

495
00:18:55,115 --> 00:18:56,615
- We're in Yeonhui-dong.
- Yes, we are.

496
00:18:56,615 --> 00:18:58,085
There's even Yeonhui-dong Barbershop.

497
00:18:58,115 --> 00:19:00,185
My favorite bakery is in Yeonhui-dong.

498
