Just because I lose to another restaurant today...

1766
01:03:14,975 --> 01:03:16,735
- doesn't mean my life is ruined.
- Of course.

1767
01:03:16,735 --> 01:03:17,775
(Her pronunciation has suddenly improved.)

1768
01:03:18,005 --> 01:03:19,945
- One minute left.
- What?

1769
01:03:20,745 --> 01:03:22,445
- One minute left?
- Yes.

1770
01:03:23,015 --> 01:03:24,985
(Meanwhile, the enemy is approaching.)

1771
01:03:25,245 --> 01:03:27,485
(A fearsome entry of burgers)

1772
01:03:27,885 --> 01:03:31,385
(The enemy takes the high ground first.)

1773
01:03:31,585 --> 01:03:32,585
Oh, my gosh.

1774
01:03:32,585 --> 01:03:35,425
(On the other hand, they have nothing ready.)

1775
01:03:35,625 --> 01:03:36,895
(Current time: 8:45pm)

1776
01:03:36,895 --> 01:03:38,965
(Time's up.)

1777
01:03:38,965 --> 01:03:40,525
(And...)

1778
01:03:40,525 --> 01:03:41,935
(The dinner announcement has been sent.)

1779
01:03:41,935 --> 01:03:43,695
(There are burgers on the 2nd floor! Enjoy your meal.)

1780
01:03:43,965 --> 01:03:47,805
(The tasting panelists enter one after another in hunger.)

1781
01:03:48,205 --> 01:03:51,705
(To the place where there's too much rice cake in burgers)

1782
01:03:51,745 --> 01:03:53,505
(They approach closer.)

1783
01:03:53,705 --> 01:03:55,645
Let's serve a few of them together.

1784
01:03:55,645 --> 01:03:56,915
- We're doing well.
- We're doing well.

1785
01:03:56,915 --> 01:03:58,545
I'll just serve one.

1786
01:03:58,885 --> 01:04:00,685
- There's only one option.
- Exactly.

1787
01:04:00,785 --> 01:04:02,385
This is all?

1788
01:04:03,185 --> 01:04:04,185
It's not here.

1789
01:04:04,185 --> 01:04:05,255
(Rice cake burger isn't here.)

1790
01:04:05,525 --> 01:04:06,725
I guess I'll take this.

1791
01:04:07,055 --> 01:04:11,365
(The customers they missed in the beginning...)

1792
01:04:11,365 --> 01:04:13,595
- What's that?
- Shrimp burger.

1793
01:04:13,595 --> 01:04:16,665
(are quite many.)

1794
01:04:17,065 --> 01:04:19,605
- The last one.
- You're five minutes behind.

1795
01:04:19,965 --> 01:04:21,435
- What should we do?
- We can do it.

1796
01:04:21,435 --> 01:04:23,335
- We need to get going.
- We can do it.

1797
01:04:23,335 --> 01:04:24,945
Send the carrot rice cakes up first.

1798
01:04:24,945 --> 01:04:27,375
Can I physically block them from taking the other burgers?

1799
01:04:27,715 --> 01:04:30,615
- I think that's a good idea.
- Yu Jin, take carrot rice cakes.

1800
01:04:30,785 --> 01:04:33,015
Yu Jin, what do we do?

1801
01:04:33,385 --> 01:04:34,815
Shall we serve the ones that are done first?

1802
01:04:34,955 --> 01:04:36,855
Send the complete ones up first.

1803
01:04:36,985 --> 01:04:38,555
The meal time has started,

1804
01:04:38,555 --> 01:04:40,155
so they'll be going up one by one.

1805
01:04:40,155 --> 01:04:41,855
Guys, what do we do?

1806
01:04:41,855 --> 01:04:43,725
Yu Jin, go up with the complete ones.

1807
01:04:43,725 --> 01:04:45,825
- Do I really go up?
- Yes, go up first.

1808
01:04:46,025 --> 01:04:47,535
We need to serve something.

1809
01:04:47,535 --> 01:04:48,835
They're going up.

1810
01:04:48,935 --> 01:04:50,765
What should we do?

1811
01:04:50,765 --> 01:04:52,005
Yu Jin, what should we do?

1812
01:04:52,005 --> 01:04:53,765
- Here.
- The stairs are hard to climb,

1813
01:04:53,765 --> 01:04:55,075
so we need to bring a few more when we go up.

1814
01:04:55,075 --> 01:04:57,175
- What do we do, Yu Jin?
- Just three more.

1815
01:04:57,345 --> 01:04:58,945
- This is insane.
- You're doing great.

1816
01:04:58,945 --> 01:05:00,105
- You're doing great.
- You're doing well.

1817
01:05:00,105 --> 01:05:02,115
- What do we do?
- I'll just put one.

1818
01:05:02,515 --> 01:05:04,045
(Rushing)

1819
01:05:04,315 --> 01:05:06,485
(She moves quickly like a rabbit.)

1820
01:05:07,955 --> 01:05:10,255
Where should I set this?

1821
01:05:10,255 --> 01:05:12,055
Where should I set this? What's this?

1822
01:05:12,455 --> 01:05:14,255
Yu Jin, where do I set this?

1823
01:05:14,255 --> 01:05:16,355
(Yu Jin is on the 1st floor.)

1824
01:05:16,525 --> 01:05:18,165
You should eat tasty food.

1825
01:05:18,365 --> 01:05:19,825
A burger made of rice cake.

1826
01:05:20,025 --> 01:05:21,965
(She manages to serve it somehow.)

1827
01:05:21,995 --> 01:05:24,465
Yu Jin... Hello.

1828
01:05:24,765 --> 01:05:25,935
Hello. Please hold on.

1829
01:05:25,935 --> 01:05:27,135
Our food is on the way too.

1830
01:05:27,435 --> 01:05:29,375
Ours is coming.

1831
01:05:29,635 --> 01:05:30,845
Hello.

1832
01:05:30,845 --> 01:05:33,075
Delicious burgers have arrived.

1833
01:05:33,075 --> 01:05:34,275
Excuse me.

1834
01:05:35,045 --> 01:05:37,715
It's really delicious. It's cute, right?

1835
01:05:37,985 --> 01:05:39,515
Enjoy.

1836
01:05:39,845 --> 01:05:42,655
(Running)

1837
01:05:42,885 --> 01:05:45,555
Now that I'm in a hurry, I can just run up the stairs.

1838
01:05:45,555 --> 01:05:47,895
Exactly. Remember what I said?

1839
01:05:48,095 --> 01:05:49,325
I just end up doing it.

1840
01:05:49,895 --> 01:05:51,495
(1 rice cake burger)

1841
01:05:51,825 --> 01:05:53,165
(2 rice cake burgers)

1842
01:05:53,465 --> 01:05:54,895
(Although they're late,)

1843
01:05:54,895 --> 01:05:56,335
(Space Rice Cake's burgers are catching up.)

1844
01:05:56,465 --> 01:05:58,465
You've exceeded ten minutes.

1845
01:05:58,465 --> 01:05:59,665
Shall we go up one more time?

1846
01:05:59,665 --> 01:06:01,375
- Please go one more time.
- One more time.

1847
01:06:01,475 --> 01:06:03,705
(She hurriedly goes to deliver.)

1848
01:06:03,975 --> 01:06:06,305
Gosh, you should try this.

1849
01:06:06,805 --> 01:06:08,615
(But...)

1850
01:06:08,775 --> 01:06:11,045
- I want to try the shrimp burger.
- Me too.

1851
01:06:11,045 --> 01:06:12,315
(Shrimp burgers are still nowhere to be seen.)

1852
01:06:13,245 --> 01:06:14,485
This is cardio.

1853
01:06:14,485 --> 01:06:16,355
(Shrimp burgers are coming.)

1854
01:06:16,485 --> 01:06:18,385
- Shrimp burgers.
- They're warm.

1855
01:06:18,655 --> 01:06:21,355
If you wait a little longer, you can get warm shrimp burgers.

1856
01:06:22,055 --> 01:06:25,625
If you want shrimp burgers, please wait for a bit.

1857
01:06:25,995 --> 01:06:27,635
Shrimp burgers on the way.

1858
01:06:28,435 --> 01:06:30,635
You want more shrimp burgers?

1859
01:06:30,835 --> 01:06:31,935
Director.

1860
01:06:32,735 --> 01:06:34,005
Your shrimp burger.

1861
01:06:34,005 --> 01:06:35,075
(She's practically a shrimp burger ambassador.)

1862
01:06:35,075 --> 01:06:37,275
Who wants shrimp burgers?

1863
01:06:38,305 --> 01:06:40,945
(Thanks to the ambassador, shrimp burgers are popular.)

1864
01:06:41,045 --> 01:06:43,015
Most of the staff have gone up.

1865
01:06:43,015 --> 01:06:46,085
Only the cameramen here are left.

1866
01:06:46,585 --> 01:06:48,185
- Our team.
- Please go.

1867
01:06:48,185 --> 01:06:49,215
Uno, Dos, Cuatro...

1868
01:06:49,315 --> 01:06:51,355
Please make a good choice.

1869
01:06:51,355 --> 01:06:52,525
We worked hard!

1870
01:06:52,985 --> 01:06:54,955
(Meanwhile, Cameraman Cuatro faces the burger he always shot.)

1871
01:06:55,395 --> 01:06:57,425
You want a shrimp burger, don't you?

1872
01:06:57,965 --> 01:07:00,495
Freshly made shrimp burger. Enjoy!

1873
01:07:00,895 --> 01:07:02,235
(Delivery complete)

1874
01:07:02,495 --> 01:07:04,905
(Delayed by 13 minutes)

1875
01:07:05,435 --> 01:07:08,405
I feel like I'm losing weight.

1876
01:07:10,205 --> 01:07:12,845
- I don't know. I think...
- Now, you...

1877
01:07:13,875 --> 01:07:15,945
can take a break and wait for the reviews.

1878
01:07:15,945 --> 01:07:16,975
- Okay.
- Okay.

1879
01:07:17,245 --> 01:07:19,085
He brought it here.

1880
01:07:19,915 --> 01:07:20,915
You're going to eat it in front of us?

1881
01:07:21,615 --> 01:07:22,855
They can make their reviews like that.

1882
01:07:22,855 --> 01:07:23,885
Don't spill it.

1883
01:07:25,825 --> 01:07:26,885
Are you done?

1884
01:07:27,555 --> 01:07:28,825
- The bread and...
- Are you done?

1885
01:07:28,825 --> 01:07:30,025
- Do you want more?
- No thanks.

1886
01:07:30,025 --> 01:07:31,765
- Do you need a refill?
- I'm fine.

1887
01:07:31,765 --> 01:07:32,795
- You're fine?
- I had enough.

1888
01:07:32,925 --> 01:07:35,295
- Tell me if you need more.
- You don't give refills.

1889
01:07:35,295 --> 01:07:37,195
I have more hash browns here.

1890
01:07:37,535 --> 01:07:39,965
We're slow, but the food tastes good.

1891
01:07:42,775 --> 01:07:44,475
They're writing negative comments.

1892
01:07:44,505 --> 01:07:46,105
- Their reviews...
- Are you writing negative comments?

1893
01:07:46,105 --> 01:07:47,715
They are writing their reviews. They're criticizing us.

1894
01:07:47,715 --> 01:07:49,115
- Where are they?
- Right in front of us.

1895
01:07:50,275 --> 01:07:51,285
(Monitoring the cameramen)

1896
01:07:51,285 --> 01:07:53,185
They're done eating.

1897
01:07:53,845 --> 01:07:56,215
(Just then)

1898
01:07:56,515 --> 01:07:58,185
(Do desserts not come with spoons?)

1899
01:07:58,355 --> 01:07:59,525
(I also don't have a spoon.)

1900
01:07:59,525 --> 01:08:00,685
(Neither do I! How are we supposed to eat this?)

1901
01:08:00,685 --> 01:08:02,395
(They made a critical mistake.)

1902
01:08:02,755 --> 01:08:03,995
The shrimp burgers...

1903
01:08:03,995 --> 01:08:05,995
Did you not serve the carrot dessert with spoons?

1904
01:08:09,895 --> 01:08:11,565
(The panelists would be eating like cranes now.)

1905
01:08:11,565 --> 01:08:13,465
- This is beef, right?
- Yes.

1906
01:08:13,635 --> 01:08:15,875
The shovels are here. We forgot these.

1907
01:08:16,175 --> 01:08:17,745
- We were in a rush.
- That's right.

1908
01:08:17,745 --> 01:08:18,845
(Feeling bad)

1909
01:08:19,275 --> 01:08:20,405
I'm sorry!

1910
01:08:20,405 --> 01:08:22,715
(The evaluation begins.)

1911
01:08:22,945 --> 01:08:24,815
- I'm so nervous.
- Goodness.

1912
01:08:24,915 --> 01:08:25,945
Will we hear them here?

1913
01:08:25,945 --> 01:08:26,945
(Wobbling)

1914
01:08:26,945 --> 01:08:28,515
Goodness. You must be so anxious.

1915
01:08:28,515 --> 01:08:30,215
Should we go back a step?

1916
01:08:30,215 --> 01:08:32,525
How anxious is he that he's shaking so much?

1917
01:08:32,525 --> 01:08:34,425
(Putting on a brave face out of anxiety)

1918
01:08:34,425 --> 01:08:36,155
Despite the friendship we've built...

1919
01:08:36,155 --> 01:08:39,425
First, the reason they chose burgers from outside.

1920
01:08:40,265 --> 01:08:41,795
This is a shared opinion.

1921
01:08:42,535 --> 01:08:43,535
Because ours comes out late.

1922
01:08:44,365 --> 01:08:45,935
They chose to get burgers from outside...

1923
01:08:45,935 --> 01:08:47,505
because ours comes out late.

1924
01:08:48,105 --> 01:08:50,575
We can't do anything about that because we learned it just today.

1925
01:08:50,575 --> 01:08:52,105
No restaurant learns a menu in one day...

1926
01:08:52,105 --> 01:08:53,645
- That's right.
- and starts prepping right away.

1927
01:08:53,745 --> 01:08:57,075
Right. This is an opinion by one of the producers.

1928
01:08:57,315 --> 01:09:00,385
"I wanted a rice cake burger, but it took so long to come out."

1929
01:09:01,485 --> 01:09:03,315
This is from the fixed-camera team.

1930
01:09:03,315 --> 01:09:04,355
"I couldn't eat it..."

1931
01:09:04,355 --> 01:09:05,385
- "because it came out so late."
- The fixed-camera team.

1932
01:09:05,385 --> 01:09:06,385
You couldn't eat because you were filming it,

1933
01:09:06,385 --> 01:09:07,385
not because it came out late.

1934
01:09:07,825 --> 01:09:09,625
Those were the comments.

1935
01:09:09,955 --> 01:09:10,965
What about the comments on the taste?

1936
01:09:10,965 --> 01:09:12,995
The comments on the taste.

1937
01:09:13,925 --> 01:09:15,365
This is from a writer.

1938
01:09:15,365 --> 01:09:16,735
Beef burger, four stars.

1939
01:09:17,195 --> 01:09:18,205
- Four.
- Four?

1940
01:09:18,205 --> 01:09:20,105
"The beef patty was twice as big as the ones outside."

1941
01:09:20,305 --> 01:09:22,105
"It'd be a waste not to eat it. It still tastes good when cold"

1942
01:09:22,175 --> 01:09:24,035
(The first positive comment)

1943
01:09:24,035 --> 01:09:26,675
The beef burger really got cold.

1944
01:09:26,775 --> 01:09:28,815
Still, they gave us a good evaluation. Thank you.

1945
01:09:29,275 --> 01:09:30,745
This is also from a writer.

1946
01:09:31,015 --> 01:09:33,245
Beef burger, five stars.

1947
01:09:34,385 --> 01:09:37,485
The chewy rice cake made it more fun to eat than a burger with bread.

1948
01:09:37,585 --> 01:09:39,985
- It has an interesting texture.
- Right. It has a fun texture.

1949
01:09:40,155 --> 01:09:41,995
Those were the good comments.

1950
01:09:42,395 --> 01:09:43,655
- Is that all?
- Now come...

1951
01:09:43,655 --> 01:09:44,895
- the so-so comments.
- The so-so ones.

1952
01:09:45,095 --> 01:09:46,125
It's from the camera team.

1953
01:09:46,965 --> 01:09:49,295
"It tasted great considering how it was made."

1954
01:09:49,295 --> 01:09:50,365
(Cameraman in charge of Young Ji)

1955
01:09:50,365 --> 01:09:51,905
"The shrimp patty also tasted good."

1956
01:09:52,335 --> 01:09:54,105
"Even though I usually like wasabi, it was still too sharp."

1957
01:09:54,375 --> 01:09:56,535
"It would have been nice if the fries were crispier."

1958
01:09:56,905 --> 01:09:59,905
He saw the process of making the rice cakes from the very front.

1959
01:10:00,205 --> 01:10:01,915
He would have had so many doubts when we were making it.

1960
01:10:01,915 --> 01:10:03,645
- But it tasted good, right?
- What a relief.

1961
01:10:03,645 --> 01:10:05,745
- Tasty, right? Weren't you shocked?
- It's such a relief.

1962
01:10:05,985 --> 01:10:08,415
This is also...

1963
01:10:08,415 --> 01:10:09,585
- an ambiguous review.
- Ambiguous.

1964
01:10:09,715 --> 01:10:12,155
There are four stars, though. It's from the camera team.

1965
01:10:13,125 --> 01:10:14,495
I chose it because I was curious...

1966
01:10:14,495 --> 01:10:15,855
after seeing the process from the very front.

1967
01:10:15,855 --> 01:10:16,895
(Cameraman in charge of Mimi)

1968
01:10:16,895 --> 01:10:17,995
"I was satisfied..."

1969
01:10:17,995 --> 01:10:19,995
"with the crispiness of the shrimp patty."

1970
01:10:19,995 --> 01:10:21,495
"It tasted good because it had a lot of shrimp."

1971
01:10:21,495 --> 01:10:22,535
(Cameraman in charge of Mimi)

1972
01:10:22,535 --> 01:10:25,605
"I was disappointed because the rice cake bun fell apart,"

1973
01:10:25,605 --> 01:10:26,965
- "which made it difficult to eat."
- Oh, no.

1974
01:10:26,965 --> 01:10:28,375
- I'm sorry. We'll try to fix that.
- At the end...

1975
01:10:28,375 --> 01:10:29,805
- At the end...
- That's what it says.

1976
01:10:29,805 --> 01:10:31,275
We rushed at the end.

1977
01:10:32,345 --> 01:10:34,145
From the fixed-camera team,

1978
01:10:34,515 --> 01:10:36,145
this person chose the beef burger.

1979
01:10:36,475 --> 01:10:38,215
"I wonder if the person who made it chopped onions before."

1980
01:10:38,215 --> 01:10:39,645
"I smell onions even though there are no onions."

1981
01:10:39,645 --> 01:10:40,685
My goodness.

1982
01:10:40,685 --> 01:10:42,055
- How did that person know that?
- That's the worst.

1983
01:10:42,585 --> 01:10:44,425
- Did you do it right after that?
- This is a bit sad.

1984
01:10:44,425 --> 01:10:45,485
- Right.
- Goodness.

1985
01:10:45,485 --> 01:10:47,655
- We have to think about that.
- I should use this.

1986
01:10:47,855 --> 01:10:50,495
Those were the overall comments on the burgers.

1987
01:10:50,595 --> 01:10:51,965
(Evaluations on the rice cake burgers: Better than expected...)

1988
01:10:51,965 --> 01:10:53,325
(considering how it was made, but often with a strong onion smell)

1989
01:10:53,725 --> 01:10:55,695
- Moving on to the carrot cake.
- Carrot cake.

1990
01:10:55,895 --> 01:10:57,065
- Carrot cake.
- We forgot to serve...

1991
01:10:57,065 --> 01:10:58,205
the shovels with the carrot cakes.

1992
01:10:58,205 --> 01:11:01,405
Forgetting to serve the shovels... Isn't that like picking a fight?

1993
01:11:01,405 --> 01:11:02,975
- Help yourselves.
- Help yourselves.

1994
01:11:04,005 --> 01:11:06,945
These are the comments.

1995
01:11:07,405 --> 01:11:10,375
"What I liked was the refreshing and tasty mint cream."

1996
01:11:10,945 --> 01:11:12,745
"But I almost ate with my hands..."

1997
01:11:12,745 --> 01:11:14,555
"because it wasn't served with a shovel spoon."

1998
01:11:15,055 --> 01:11:16,885
"It also had a strong chocolate flavor..."

1999
01:11:16,885 --> 01:11:18,325
"because there wasn't enough gijeongtteok and castella."

2000
01:11:18,425 --> 01:11:20,685
- I'm sorry.
- That's right. We did that.

2001
01:11:21,225 --> 01:11:22,225
Also...

2002
01:11:22,795 --> 01:11:24,965
This is from the fixed-camera team.

2003
01:11:25,595 --> 01:11:28,995
"I didn't take the carrot cake because I don't like mint."

2004
01:11:29,235 --> 01:11:30,235
(A review expressing a dislike)

2005
01:11:30,235 --> 01:11:31,335
- Do you like mint?
- Some people don't like it.

2006
01:11:31,335 --> 01:11:33,265
But it could taste good once you try it.

2007
01:11:33,265 --> 01:11:34,835
- I should say that tomorrow.
- That's right.

2008
01:11:35,805 --> 01:11:39,145
A writer gave three stars and commented...

2009
01:11:39,145 --> 01:11:41,005
It must be a negative one.

2010
01:11:41,005 --> 01:11:43,215
"It was filled lower than the cup,"

2011
01:11:43,215 --> 01:11:45,585
"so I wondered if they had gone light with the ingredients,"

2012
01:11:45,585 --> 01:11:47,485
"but everything balanced out well when eaten together."

2013
01:11:47,485 --> 01:11:48,655
That's a relief. It tasted good.

2014
01:11:48,655 --> 01:11:49,785
- Right.
- It tasted good.

2015
01:11:49,785 --> 01:11:52,055
And this...

2016
01:11:52,355 --> 01:11:54,595
